    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0069" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/5–2340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Keith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-23T21:00:00-05:00">May 23, 1940—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 24—12:53 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>120. Department’s telegram No. 84, May 23, noon.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d73-f1"/>
                    I have just returned from interview with Foreign Minister<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d73-f2"/> at his home. He <pb facs="0070" n="58" xml:id="pg58"/>
                    personally fully approves rapid carrying out of proposed plan but cannot give me
                    official answer until after seeing President<anchor n="81" xml:id="d73-f3"/>
                    tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Keith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
